    <briefdescription>
<para>Canopy Photolysis Module. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This module contains subroutines for calculating photolysis attenuation within forest canopies based on the algorithms described in Makar et al. (2017). The module computes how photolysis rates are reduced within the canopy due to shading by leaves and branches.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Patrick C. Campbell </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>June 2022</para>
</simplesect>
\references Makar, P., Staebler, R., Akingunola, A. et al. The effects of forest canopy shading and turbulence on boundary layer ozone. Nat Commun 8, 15243 (2017). <ulink url="https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms15243">https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms15243</ulink> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
